## A5. H1 and H2 using selected labels

We now test the old representation, rather than assuming that any observed label change proves a persona effect.

- **H1:** pool human votes within each text and persona comparison, enumerate all assignments to the observed condition sizes, and obtain the conditional chance of changing the selected label. Simulate the aggregate reference across texts 10,000 times. Holm correction covers the six category × persona tests.
- **H2:** preserve each model's identity and enumerate swaps of its paired neutral/persona answers. Simulate the mean ensemble-label-change rate across cells 10,000 times. Holm correction covers the two persona tests.

Green points show observed rates and text-bootstrap intervals; orange crosses show conditional-null means. The printed p-values are adjusted. These are one-sided tests of a larger change statistic, conditional on the exchangeability assumptions. Independent shuffles across human texts or model configurations are not automatically justified by text-clustered intervals.
