'''),md('''
## C6. H3 again: raw TV and a conditional-null sensitivity

First ask whether author-relevant texts have larger raw TV. Then ask whether the difference remains after subtracting each text's expected TV under pooled-vote reassignment.

Small samples from a dispersed distribution can differ even under this reference. Category definitions already involve ambiguity, so raw TV may reflect that sampling property as well as framing-associated movement.

`Observed − expected conditional TV` is a **reference-adjusted statistic**, not the identified causal part attributable to persona information. The sensitivity is post hoc. Failure to reject is not equivalence, and we keep both analyses visible.
