## C7. H4 again: magnitude and direction are now distinct

**Magnitude:** compare human and model mean TV for each text. The paired difference and interval describe this dataset and its two sampling processes.

**Direction:** compare human and model delta vectors for the same text, persona side and configuration. Cosine is +1 for aligned directions, 0 for perpendicular directions and −1 for opposite directions. If either vector is zero, direction is undefined.

We retain persona A and B separately rather than averaging their deltas before cosine. The mean is over defined comparison-level cosines; intervals resample complete text profiles. The shuffled reference permutes model text profiles as blocks, preserving their two sides and six configurations. It tests text-specific correspondence, not causation.
